# Filament / Livewire gotchas (do not regress)

We keep rediscovering the same Filament **cache / configure timing / modal** bugs. Treat these as required checklist items whenever you touch Filament pages, header actions, tables, or confirmation modals.

## 0. Page header actions are icon-only (app standard)

Page header actions and header `ActionGroup`s are **icon-only** with a tooltip from the label. Do not ship labeled header buttons (`->button()` with visible text) on page headers.

- Extend `App\Filament\Pages\Page` (not `Filament\Pages\Page`) — it normalizes headers via `TableHeaderIconAction::normalize()`
- Or call `TableHeaderIconAction::apply()` / `applyGroup()` / `applyMany()` explicitly (table toolbars already do)
- Always set `->icon(...)` and a meaningful `->label(...)` (label becomes the tooltip)

Reference: `App\Filament\Pages\Page`, `TableHeaderIconAction`, Delinquency / Automation headers.

## 1. Header actions are cached — rebuild after visibility drivers change

`getHeaderActions()` is cached on the Livewire component. Changing a property alone does **not** rebuild that cache.

Prefer a **single toggle action** whose label/icon/color are closures over two mutually exclusive `visible()` actions (pause vs resume) — header morphing often fails to swap icon buttons cleanly.

After tab or state changes: `refreshHeaderActions()` + `forceRender()` when needed.

Reference: `InteractsWithJobsTable::refreshHeaderActions()`, `toggle_scheduler`.

## 2. Tables with different columns per tab

When rebuilding a table for a side tab:

1. Clear `$this->tableColumns = []` and `$this->cachedDefaultTableColumnState = null`
2. **Then** call `$this->initTableColumnManager()`

**Never** init the column manager and clear afterward.

**Symptom if wrong:** rows show **selection checkboxes only**.

## 3. HasTable pages skip page action modals (clicks do nothing)

Filament’s page layout only renders `<x-filament-actions::modals />` when the page does **not** implement `HasTable` (`vendor/filament/filament/resources/views/components/page/index.blade.php`). Tables include their own modals host — but custom workspace pages that **conditionally hide** `{{ $this->table }}` (Status / Schedule / Overview / templates / tiers) leave **no modal host in the DOM**.

**Symptom:** header / workspace actions with `requiresConfirmation()` mount in Livewire but the browser shows **no confirmation at all** (looks like the click did nothing). Cross-browser.

**Fix:** always include the shared partial at the end of the page view:

`@include('filament.tenant.partials.page-workspace-action-modals')`

Safe when the table is also rendered — `hasActionsModalRendered` prevents a duplicate host.

Pest: on the **non-table** default tab, `assertSeeHtml('wire:partial="action-modals"')`.

Reference: Jobs, Delinquency, Audit & System, Reconciliation, Communications, Loan queue workbench.

## 4. Confirm modals — app-wide delinquency-style chrome

Every `requiresConfirmation()` action is wired in `AppServiceProvider` via `TenantPortalActionModal::applyConfirmation()` on **tenant, member, and admin** panels.

UI standard (matches delinquency check):

- Native Filament heading / description / icon (centered)
- Compact card window + equal-width Cancel / Confirm
- Field-less confirms: `formWrapper(false)` + `modalAutofocus(false)`
- Long-running only: progress footer (“Ready to run” → “Working…”) via `longRunning()` / `longRunningMessage()`
- Shared CSS: `resources/css/filament/confirm-modals.css` (imported by all panel themes)

`Action::configureUsing()` runs inside `Action::make()` **before** `->requiresConfirmation()` / `->longRunning()`. Defer modal wiring with `bootUsing()`.

### `modalSubmitAction` parameter must be named `$action`

```php
->modalSubmitAction(fn (Action $action) => $action->color('danger'));
```

Filament injects the **footer submit button** by the parameter name `action`. A differently named `Action $submit` receives the **parent** action by type-hint, so Confirm becomes the original action (auto-runs / no Confirm).

After PHP/CSS changes: `php artisan optimize:clear`, `npm run build`, `systemctl reload php8.4-fpm`.


## 5. Single primary row-click actions — seed then clear `recordActions`

`TableRecordActionGroups::configureSinglePrimaryActionRowClick()` must seed `recordActions([$action])` before `recordAction($name)` + `recordActions([])`. Otherwise Livewire throws `Public method [view] not found`.

## Checklist (new or edited Filament UI)

- [ ] Page extends `App\Filament\Pages\Page` (icon-only headers)
- [ ] Header actions have icons + labels (tooltip); no labeled header buttons
- [ ] Tab / visibility change → `refreshHeaderActions()` when actions are tab- or state-scoped
- [ ] Tab change → clear column state **before** `initTableColumnManager()`
- [ ] `HasTable` page that can hide the table → include `page-workspace-action-modals`
- [ ] Long-running confirm → `longRunning()` + progress footer; never custom body + hidden header
- [ ] `requiresConfirmation()` gets app-wide confirm chrome (bootUsing / TenantPortalActionModal)
- [ ] View-only row click → `TableRecordActionGroups::apply` / `wrap`
- [ ] Pest: icon-only headers; `action-modals` on non-table tabs; confirm mounts with progress footer; scheduler toggle; columns after tab switch
